WEBVTT

00:03.160 --> 00:06.770
Fight for your justice,
show your courage.

00:06.770 --> 00:10.370
Right! Grasp truth in these hands.

00:10.370 --> 00:13.780
Fight for your justice, I want you

00:13.780 --> 00:21.200
as you fight through
with your head held up high.

00:35.860 --> 00:39.930
Rather than polishing diamonds

00:43.040 --> 00:46.970
give me a glistening future.

00:50.250 --> 00:52.480
Even if nothing's there, get up.

00:52.480 --> 00:56.350
It's important to turn on the switch.

00:57.450 --> 01:00.220
Something new that I don't want to yield.

01:00.220 --> 01:04.750
Seeking it is justice!

01:06.360 --> 01:09.930
Fight for your justice,
be serious about it.

01:09.930 --> 01:13.540
Right! Face reality head on.

01:13.540 --> 01:16.940
Fight for your justice,
I love how you

01:16.940 --> 01:27.340
never give up even if
the current is against you.

01:31.020 --> 01:34.990
Medical log, Duero McFile recording.

01:34.990 --> 01:38.030
It has been 3 days since
we landed on this planet.

01:38.030 --> 01:39.530
Not only the inhabitants...

01:39.530 --> 01:45.630
but every living thing
on this planet is diseased.

01:45.630 --> 01:49.670
The environment has obviously
been altered on purpose.

01:49.670 --> 01:54.110
I believe this planet is an
ecological experiment by Earth.

01:54.110 --> 01:56.640
We have used heavy protection
to prevent contamination.

01:56.640 --> 02:03.450
But those born on this land are being
eaten alive from the moment of birth...

02:03.450 --> 02:07.590
...by the polluted air
and earth and toxic water.

02:07.590 --> 02:11.290
What treatment we can give
can only be a momentary solace.

02:12.730 --> 02:14.700
As someone practicing medicine...

02:14.700 --> 02:17.630
No, as one human...

02:17.630 --> 02:20.860
I feel nothing but anger
for what Earth is doing.

02:22.340 --> 02:24.140
No good.

02:24.140 --> 02:27.080
We have to terraform
this from scratch.

02:27.080 --> 02:28.610
How about over there?

02:28.610 --> 02:30.210
We've got the atmosphere all right.

02:30.210 --> 02:32.980
Okay, then let's experiment a few times.

02:32.980 --> 02:34.220
Keep it there! Thanks!

02:34.220 --> 02:35.550
All right.

02:36.850 --> 02:38.020
You know...

02:38.020 --> 02:39.010
What?

02:40.190 --> 02:42.320
We're all alone.

02:42.320 --> 02:44.430
S-So what?

02:44.430 --> 02:46.660
No matter what happens here...

02:46.660 --> 02:49.100
we're the only ones
that'll know, right?

02:49.100 --> 02:51.070
What are you thinking?

02:51.070 --> 02:52.870
Don't come over here!

02:52.870 --> 02:55.400
You know, I've been getting
interested in men lately.

02:55.400 --> 02:56.870
- Stop it! Stay away!
- Oh, it's all right.

02:56.870 --> 02:58.910
Hey, old lady! What are you doing?

02:58.910 --> 03:00.410
Who are you calling an old lady?

03:00.410 --> 03:02.310
Are you okay, Mr. Alien?

03:02.310 --> 03:04.650
Did she do something strange to you?

03:04.650 --> 03:06.350
What do you mean something strange?

03:06.350 --> 03:07.340
Like...

03:08.520 --> 03:10.850
- Don't!
- Get away from him!

03:10.850 --> 03:12.410
I've had enough of this!

03:21.800 --> 03:23.500
Well...

03:23.500 --> 03:25.730
Let's return him to the soil.

03:25.730 --> 03:28.300
We can't do that.

03:28.300 --> 03:31.300
The caskets are collected by Earth.

03:32.440 --> 03:36.110
They are carried automatically to
the mountaintop with that contraption...

03:36.110 --> 03:41.120
where they are collected by a
cargo ship that comes every so often.

03:41.120 --> 03:42.420
Unbelievable.

03:42.420 --> 03:46.090
That... is the rule of this land.

03:46.090 --> 03:52.230
Because they can't leave corpses,
people spend their lives making dolls.

03:52.230 --> 03:56.200
Those dolls alone are proof that
they have lived on this planet...

03:56.200 --> 04:00.870
and the place where their soul
resides after it loses its body.

04:00.870 --> 04:05.640
Seeing only pain,
the fire of the extinguished souls...

04:05.640 --> 04:08.910
are never passed on to others.

04:10.780 --> 04:14.080
And so, the male ship and
the female ship fused together.

04:14.080 --> 04:16.920
On top of that,
a mysterious ship was attacking.

04:16.920 --> 04:19.090
That's when I turned
the situation around.

04:19.090 --> 04:21.060
How?

04:21.060 --> 04:25.290
Well, it was a plan that
only I could have thought of.

04:25.290 --> 04:27.900
We jumped over space!

04:27.900 --> 04:32.430
Shirley, how do you think
jumping over space feels?

04:32.430 --> 04:33.900
Is it painful?

04:33.900 --> 04:36.070
No, it's surprising!

04:36.070 --> 04:38.010
Oh no!

04:38.010 --> 04:38.840
Exactly!

04:38.840 --> 04:41.280
I was the one that was surprised!

04:41.280 --> 04:43.810
When someone lies that audaciously...

04:43.810 --> 04:46.010
I don't even feel like scolding them.

04:46.010 --> 04:48.220
But I feel sorry for her.

04:48.220 --> 04:49.320
That girl.

04:49.320 --> 04:54.220
I heard she's been in this quarantine
ward ever since she was born.

04:54.220 --> 04:58.250
I guess we should let
her hear a tall tale or two.

05:01.460 --> 05:04.330
I've requested supplies to
replenish what you lack here.

05:04.330 --> 05:05.770
They should arrive tomorrow.

05:05.770 --> 05:09.470
Will everyone be better then, ribbit?

05:09.470 --> 05:12.270
I feel sorry for everyone.

05:12.270 --> 05:14.010
We're doing our best, but...

05:14.010 --> 05:15.940
Y-You know...

05:15.940 --> 05:18.010
I just thought of this...

05:18.010 --> 05:21.380
...but how about we take
these people back to Tarak?

05:21.380 --> 05:25.820
Unfortunately, we don't have enough
supplies on our ship for that.

05:25.820 --> 05:30.430
And a long voyage will only
decrease their physical stamina.

05:30.430 --> 05:33.160
I-I see.

05:33.160 --> 05:34.760
That's true.

05:34.760 --> 05:36.460
Well, excuse me.

05:36.460 --> 05:38.130
See ya...

05:44.370 --> 05:46.110
"Medicine"

05:46.110 --> 05:48.370
"Advanced Human Anatomy"

05:53.750 --> 05:56.280
This is the fifth time already.

05:56.280 --> 05:58.490
Mr. Alien, are you suffering?

05:58.490 --> 06:00.250
Y-You've gotta be kidding.

06:00.250 --> 06:01.920
This is nothing...

06:01.920 --> 06:03.490
I can't take it anymore...

06:03.490 --> 06:06.760
That old hag's at it again!

06:06.760 --> 06:08.700
Mr. Alien...

06:08.700 --> 06:11.670
Are those two all right?

06:11.670 --> 06:13.070
By that, you mean...

06:13.070 --> 06:14.700
Although it's intermittent...

06:14.700 --> 06:17.970
they've been holding the
planet for quite a while now.

06:17.970 --> 06:19.310
According to Parfet...

06:19.310 --> 06:23.280
it depends on their willpower
and the condition of the Paksis.

06:23.280 --> 06:26.410
The Paksis, huh?

06:26.410 --> 06:29.280
I heard this environment was created...

06:29.280 --> 06:32.850
by the intentional
destruction of Paksis data.

06:32.850 --> 06:37.020
Sometimes, it makes me wonder
exactly what this substance is.

06:37.020 --> 06:38.330
Me too.

06:38.330 --> 06:42.800
I had thought that it was the
ideal energy system until now.

06:42.800 --> 06:46.560
But sometimes, I feel as though
it has a will of its own.

06:57.010 --> 06:59.910
Shirley, what did you just hide?

06:59.910 --> 07:02.120
N-Nothing.

07:02.120 --> 07:03.750
Good morning, Big Brother.

07:03.750 --> 07:06.720
What? You're being so bashful, Shirley.

07:06.720 --> 07:08.690
We're good friends now, right?

07:08.690 --> 07:11.160
T-That's true...

07:11.160 --> 07:13.960
But don't laugh.

07:13.960 --> 07:15.620
See?

07:17.830 --> 07:18.870
This...

07:18.870 --> 07:20.070
That's right.

07:20.070 --> 07:21.940
It's a doll of you.

07:21.940 --> 07:25.640
I'm not that good, so I'm embarrassed.

07:25.640 --> 07:27.740
Big Brother?

07:27.740 --> 07:29.910
Well...

07:29.910 --> 07:32.310
But this doesn't have any hair.

07:32.310 --> 07:33.480
It's all right!

07:33.480 --> 07:36.750
See, I'm going to sew it on later.

07:36.750 --> 07:37.820
I'm glad.

07:37.820 --> 07:40.420
Make it look as
handsome as the real thing.

07:40.420 --> 07:44.630
If you do, I'll pay you back by
granting any wish you have, Shirley.

07:44.630 --> 07:46.290
Really?

07:47.200 --> 07:48.230
But...

07:48.230 --> 07:50.230
It's all right!

07:50.230 --> 07:56.570
Now, ask anything of humble,
little Bart, Lady Shirley.

07:56.570 --> 07:59.040
Well, then...

07:59.040 --> 08:03.610
You know, I want to climb
onto the top of that dome.

08:03.610 --> 08:09.520
Just once, I want to go outside,
and I want to look far away from here.

08:09.520 --> 08:13.960
The only sky I can see from
this window is all gray.

08:13.960 --> 08:16.860
All right, gotcha!

08:16.860 --> 08:18.460
I'll take you there.

08:18.460 --> 08:19.630
Really?

08:19.630 --> 08:20.900
But in return...

08:20.900 --> 08:24.400
Even if it hurts, you have to
do your best and get treated.

08:24.400 --> 08:25.770
Okay?

08:25.770 --> 08:26.730
Okay.

08:26.730 --> 08:29.070
That's right. About your doll...

08:29.070 --> 08:32.210
I didn't get something...

08:32.210 --> 08:34.540
Shirley! Hang in there!

08:36.280 --> 08:38.510
I-I'm all right...

08:39.850 --> 08:41.720
Duero! Come here!

08:41.720 --> 08:43.950
The dispersion system is on standby.

08:43.950 --> 08:45.850
We're ready here, too! Fire away!

08:45.850 --> 08:47.180
Roger!

08:53.030 --> 08:55.390
Please, let it go well...

08:59.470 --> 09:00.770
How is she?

09:00.770 --> 09:02.570
She's stable for now.

09:02.570 --> 09:04.770
What do you mean "for now"?

09:04.770 --> 09:07.710
It means she's far
from being fully cured.

09:07.710 --> 09:09.180
I can prolong her life...

09:09.180 --> 09:12.510
but her body has been
contaminated since birth.

09:12.510 --> 09:14.950
Then use my body!

09:14.950 --> 09:16.980
Take any part that you need!

09:16.980 --> 09:17.950
If Shirley can...

09:17.950 --> 09:21.560
Bart! It's not that kind of a problem.

09:21.560 --> 09:23.220
Please understand.

09:24.960 --> 09:26.930
Shirley...

09:26.930 --> 09:30.430
...was happy to hear my stories.

09:30.430 --> 09:32.800
Without blinking, seriously...

09:32.800 --> 09:38.170
It's the first time I've seen anyone
happy about something I've done.

09:38.170 --> 09:40.880
Shirley is...

09:40.880 --> 09:43.610
...one of my dearest friends.

09:45.380 --> 09:47.080
Doctor, where are you?

09:47.080 --> 09:48.080
What's wrong?

09:48.080 --> 09:49.180
Emergency patient!

09:49.180 --> 09:51.320
She collapsed on her way here.

09:51.320 --> 09:53.820
There's no answer when we talk to her.

09:53.820 --> 09:55.120
Take her to the examination table.

09:56.220 --> 09:57.830
She's pregnant.

09:57.830 --> 09:59.090
Close to giving birth, too.

09:59.090 --> 10:01.730
No matter where you go,
they're all sick.

10:01.730 --> 10:04.570
It's harder to find
someone that isn't ill.

10:04.570 --> 10:06.870
If my hunches are correct...

10:06.870 --> 10:12.670
If they avoid contamination at birth,
they won't contract the disease for life.

10:12.670 --> 10:14.340
No good at all.

10:14.340 --> 10:16.330
No good over here, either.

10:17.080 --> 10:19.880
We're trying to
change the entire planet.

10:19.880 --> 10:23.080
Perhaps we're rather full of ourselves.

10:23.080 --> 10:27.050
If we could do this, I'm sure the
problem on Mejale would be long gone.

10:27.050 --> 10:30.160
Can't we at least
quarantine the hospital alone?

10:30.160 --> 10:31.430
What do you mean?

10:31.430 --> 10:33.290
There's a baby about to be born.

10:33.290 --> 10:36.330
The doctor said they get contaminated...

10:36.330 --> 10:39.630
by contact to this planet's
atmosphere at the moment of birth.

10:39.630 --> 10:43.140
So we just make it so they don't
touch this planet's environment.

10:43.140 --> 10:45.970
But we don't have enough Paksis.

10:45.970 --> 10:48.740
Then it doesn't matter
if it only covers one bed!

10:48.740 --> 10:52.550
Let's think about procuring
a space for that baby!

10:52.550 --> 10:54.480
Got it!

10:54.480 --> 10:55.620
All right, we'll do this!

10:55.620 --> 10:56.820
Help me, you two.

10:56.820 --> 10:57.720
- All right!
- All right!

10:57.720 --> 10:59.520
Everyone, gather here!

11:03.420 --> 11:05.390
I can't take it anymore.

11:07.160 --> 11:09.360
What are you doing? Geez!

11:09.360 --> 11:11.670
I'm tired now!

11:11.670 --> 11:13.930
All right, then we'll...

11:20.270 --> 11:22.580
The enemy! They're finally here!

11:22.580 --> 11:24.010
Oh no! At a time like this?

11:29.450 --> 11:31.850
Geez, you're getting in my way!

11:31.850 --> 11:34.060
I was just getting restless!

11:34.060 --> 11:35.720
I think I'll thrash about awhile!

11:35.720 --> 11:38.630
Hibiki, Jura, you two stay put for now.

11:38.630 --> 11:40.390
Keep this planet from being invaded.

11:40.390 --> 11:41.860
You've gotta be kidding.

11:46.930 --> 11:48.600
Bart.

11:49.370 --> 11:52.270
The enemy's here.
We're going back to the Nirvana.

11:54.840 --> 11:59.780
I know how much you want to stay here,
but the ship can't move without you.

11:59.780 --> 12:01.370
Hurry.

12:04.550 --> 12:06.950
Shirley...

12:06.950 --> 12:08.620
Bart!

12:16.930 --> 12:19.000
Shirley...

12:19.000 --> 12:22.500
I'll protect you.

12:22.500 --> 12:24.160
Let's go.

12:30.510 --> 12:34.650
Dita, until Barnette joins us,
I leave command of B team to you.

12:34.650 --> 12:36.420
Can you do it?

12:36.420 --> 12:37.720
Of course!

12:37.720 --> 12:41.620
Mr. Alien isn't here,
so I'll do my best to cover for him!

12:41.620 --> 12:43.020
All right.

12:43.020 --> 12:44.590
All ships, follow me!

12:44.590 --> 12:47.120
- We'll pound the main enemy body!
- Roger!

12:52.700 --> 12:54.000
Doctor!

12:54.000 --> 12:55.370
It won't be born soon!

12:55.370 --> 12:57.440
Time the intervals between contractions!

12:57.440 --> 12:58.170
Okay.

12:58.170 --> 13:00.140
Parfet, how are you doing there?

13:00.140 --> 13:01.610
Almost there.

13:01.610 --> 13:04.080
No time to test it, but I'll do it.

13:05.280 --> 13:07.520
We'll proceed and
attack the main enemy unit!

13:07.520 --> 13:08.500
Roger!

13:14.660 --> 13:15.640
What?

13:20.560 --> 13:22.230
The enemy's getting wiser.

13:22.230 --> 13:23.400
This is C team.

13:23.400 --> 13:25.000
- Attacks aren't working!
- That's not it!

13:25.000 --> 13:25.900
Formation broken!

13:25.900 --> 13:29.140
- Hey, this is no time to play.
- Where's that delivery?

13:29.140 --> 13:31.730
I'm sorry. I'm about to hit my limit.

13:37.780 --> 13:40.110
Vandread Jura's shields are unstable!

13:40.110 --> 13:42.480
The two pilots' conditions
aren't good, either!

13:42.480 --> 13:44.920
Hibiki, Jura! Answer me!

13:44.920 --> 13:47.910
I hate to say this, but we're
starting to lose control.

13:52.460 --> 13:54.120
Oh no!

14:02.770 --> 14:04.430
Big Brother?

14:07.510 --> 14:09.010
That's right.

14:09.010 --> 14:11.530
The doll... I have to make it.

14:17.450 --> 14:19.110
Big Brother...

14:27.060 --> 14:28.100
Where?

14:28.100 --> 14:30.100
Shirley's room.

14:30.100 --> 14:31.700
Paiway, call the captain.

14:31.700 --> 14:33.500
- Ask her to do the delivery.
- Okay!

14:36.700 --> 14:40.770
Shit, I keep quiet,
and they let it get to their heads.

14:40.770 --> 14:42.110
They're coming.

14:47.480 --> 14:48.850
Dita, calm down.

14:48.850 --> 14:51.590
If you get too close,
they'll pull you in, too!

14:51.590 --> 14:53.250
But Mr. Alien...

15:05.100 --> 15:07.000
- Jura, thanks for waiting!
- Well?

15:07.000 --> 15:09.400
Do you get how stagehands feel now?

15:09.400 --> 15:11.640
Oh, Barnette!

15:11.640 --> 15:13.610
What are you talking about,
coming this late?

15:13.610 --> 15:16.480
First off, how are we gonna
win being defensive the whole time?

15:16.480 --> 15:17.980
I'll protect her.

15:17.980 --> 15:21.610
I won't let them get
even one step closer!

15:26.890 --> 15:29.820
No matter what happens,
I won't move from here!

15:31.060 --> 15:33.390
What happened to him?

15:33.390 --> 15:35.100
From your viewpoint...

15:35.100 --> 15:37.530
...they may have insignificant lives.

15:37.530 --> 15:41.100
But they're doing their best
to live them to the fullest.

15:41.100 --> 15:42.700
Shirley...

15:42.700 --> 15:44.440
I'll do my best.

15:44.440 --> 15:45.870
So...

15:45.870 --> 15:48.040
So do your best too, Shirley!

15:48.040 --> 15:51.080
Do your best! Do your best!

15:51.080 --> 15:52.610
Do your best!

15:52.610 --> 15:56.910
I'll never let you get your way!

16:10.730 --> 16:11.720
- No way!
- No way!

16:13.330 --> 16:16.360
Get away from this planet!

16:19.140 --> 16:21.200
Idiot, there are allies here!

16:26.480 --> 16:27.470
What?

16:31.520 --> 16:33.120
What a sight...

16:33.120 --> 16:35.020
What? What was that thing?

16:35.020 --> 16:37.120
It's a friendly weapon.

16:40.390 --> 16:42.390
What is that?

16:43.600 --> 16:46.330
He showed us he's a man.

17:00.980 --> 17:02.180
We're all right!

17:02.180 --> 17:05.190
The baby is healthy!

17:05.190 --> 17:06.520
We're all right here, too.

17:06.520 --> 17:08.290
The field has stabilized.

17:08.290 --> 17:10.260
Really...

17:10.260 --> 17:13.060
...I don't know how to say thanks.

17:13.060 --> 17:14.560
I-It's nothing...

17:14.560 --> 17:18.970
What I really wanted to do
was purify the entire planet.

17:18.970 --> 17:22.900
This is all we could do for now.

17:22.900 --> 17:24.510
No.

17:24.510 --> 17:26.470
This is enough.

17:26.470 --> 17:31.380
Your results mean
something important to us.

17:31.380 --> 17:37.380
You have created a sanctuary on
this wasteland.

17:37.380 --> 17:43.160
You have given us a ray of light
when we have been in pure darkness.

17:43.160 --> 17:45.830
A light called hope.

17:45.830 --> 17:50.230
It is true that this might
only be a very small space.

17:50.230 --> 17:55.170
But we can continue to deliver
children here and raise them.

17:55.170 --> 18:00.240
And the children who grow healthy can
slowly increase the sanctuary's size...

18:00.240 --> 18:06.210
and someday turn this planet
back into a beautiful, green land.

18:06.210 --> 18:10.450
Unfortunately, we will
not be able to see to it.

18:10.450 --> 18:13.490
But the light of
hope that was lit here...

18:13.490 --> 18:16.760
is sure to be passed
on to the next generation.

18:16.760 --> 18:18.590
It is all thanks to you.

18:18.590 --> 18:19.930
Thank you.

18:19.930 --> 18:21.590
Thank you so much.

18:24.130 --> 18:25.870
I'm sorry...

18:25.870 --> 18:27.530
I'm sorry.

18:31.910 --> 18:32.870
Shirley!

18:32.870 --> 18:34.530
I won...

18:46.450 --> 18:48.190
W-What's wrong?

18:48.190 --> 18:50.090
It's strangely quiet.

18:51.730 --> 18:53.960
T-The machine is turned off, too.

18:53.960 --> 18:58.070
C-Come on, this is a bad prank.

18:58.070 --> 19:00.170
Hey, Shirley...

19:00.170 --> 19:01.940
Open your eyes.

19:01.940 --> 19:03.200
I have another story...

19:03.200 --> 19:05.210
Bart.

19:05.210 --> 19:07.810
She did her best until the very end.

19:07.810 --> 19:09.540
She lived to the fullest.

19:11.110 --> 19:16.020
But I couldn't save her.

19:16.020 --> 19:17.680
I'm sorry.

19:53.850 --> 19:57.450
Is this the first time that
you've seen someone's death?

20:00.030 --> 20:02.930
It's hard. It's sad.

20:02.930 --> 20:06.700
I should have done this.
I should have done that.

20:06.700 --> 20:09.940
All that comes up
in your head are regrets.

20:09.940 --> 20:13.510
The only thing that the
people left behind can do...

20:13.510 --> 20:17.000
...is to remember them
and not to forget them.

20:18.080 --> 20:22.750
Bart, you've taken
on the flame of her soul.

20:22.750 --> 20:25.990
Your life is no longer just yours now.

20:25.990 --> 20:27.960
Now, lift your head.

20:27.960 --> 20:30.620
Embrace the memories and move forward.

20:30.620 --> 20:33.360
For her sake, as well.

20:33.360 --> 20:36.130
There's no need to hold back.

20:36.130 --> 20:38.000
Cry as much as you want.

20:38.000 --> 20:42.800
Tears you shed for others are
not something to be ashamed of.

20:54.210 --> 20:56.020
We've collected the landing party.

20:56.020 --> 20:57.680
Ready for departure!

21:14.870 --> 21:17.670
Now, we'll be taking
back the time we've lost!

21:17.670 --> 21:20.610
Full speed ahead towards our homeland!

21:20.610 --> 21:21.680
Roger that.

21:21.680 --> 21:24.010
Full speed ahead!
